{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 4, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 7147003361181695045, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 611, "mtime": 1791871728.5637534, "sha256": "a2d64a5af3a5828c39605d51cb6cc9913ee077d871d69b8d9cf87c44a44df57d"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 226, "mtime": 1791871736.6923916, "sha256": "bff83cb8356be8963f6643b5393907244e54116e53db495a24f146e17868d7fe"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/5/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/5/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. I checked it by calling the function directly and running both test functions without pytest, because pytest isn't installed here. The full suite hasn't been run.\n\n**Cause:** In `pricing/money.py`, `round_money` used `round(x, 2)`. A float can't store 2.675 exactly; it's actually 2.67499999\u2026, so it rounds down. On top of that, Python's `round()` sends exact halves to the even digit rather than always up, so it doesn't match the \"half up\" the docstring promises.\n\n**Fix:** `round_money` now converts the number to the decimal form Python prints for it (so 2.675 is treated as exactly 2.675), rounds to cents with halves always going up, and returns a float as before. Negative halves round away from zero, so -2.675 gives -2.68.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `round_money`: `2.675 \u2192 2.68`, `0.125 \u2192 0.13`, `-2.675 \u2192 -2.68`, `2.674 \u2192 2.67`, `5 \u2192 5.0`.\n- `add_vat(10)` still gives `12.0`, since it uses `round_money`.\n- The existing `tests/test_split.py::test_split` passes.\n- I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, which checks the cases above, and it passes.\n\nOne thing to know: `add_vat` rounds whatever `x * (1 + rate)` comes out as. If that multiplication itself lands slightly below an exact half-cent, the result can still round down.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 10, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 279541, "requests_cache_write": 7622, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1356462, "requests_count": 10, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 2077, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial5", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 8, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T06:08